title: The Door (2025)
permalink: the-door-2025
date: 2025-11-22
release_artist: Rishi Vanukuru

more_label: About

-- synopsis
A song about the sound of the door.
-- synopsis

-- more
If I ever get the chance to [walk around Montmartre one summer evening, playing the guitar and singing a song](https://youtu.be/f845_v41YFo), this would be the song.

Words:

My heart sings at the sight of your smile
We both say the words, it's been a while
The world it makes sense for a moment or three
But then we're reminded 
That I will soon leave

Applause from a few streets across
Punctutates arguments you never lost
An unknowing audience somehow kept time
With the rhythms of all of our punches and lines

What can I do but apologize
For this merry-go-round of hellos and goodbyes
I wish I was better at bridging this distance
I meant it when I said I'll miss this

Your heart sinks at the sound of the door
I leave with a promise that I will return
I remember the tears that fell
And I wonder, 
were they for the promise, 
or for the farewell

Was I 
Always a project, a puzzle you found, at a
Thrift store one morning in April, a gamble
The pieces were missing 
before you came looking 
We both wish that we could have known

If it was
Always so perfect, what wasn't working
What changed when I left two summers ago
Was it the silence of my absence 
Or the silence of the door

Was I 
Always a project, a puzzle you found, at a
Thrift store one morning in April, a gamble
The pieces were missing 
And soon you stopped looking 
We both wish that we could have known

If it was
Always so perfect, what wasn't working
What changed when I left two summers ago
Was it the silence of my absence 
Or the silence of the door

I'll never know


-- more

